      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Visual evoked potentials (VEP) were studied in 16 persons with radiological confirmed Kimmerle anomaly. Each eye was stimulated by the reversible checker-board pattern using the reversal and flash stimulation methods. Abnormal responses were noted in about 75% of the studied patients. Latency disturbances prevailed during reversal stimulation and abnormal configuration of responses predominated during flash stimulation."},
